--- title Tuples
--- about A tuple is a run of bytes written with dots, which is what
--- about makes it right for a version or a colour. The part worth
--- about pinning is that arithmetic on one clamps at each end rather
--- about than wrapping, so a segment never leaves 0 to 255.

--- id tuples/adding-to-every-segment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold 1.2.3 + 1
--- result
"2.3.4"

--- id tuples/subtracting-from-every-segment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold 1.2.3 - 1
--- result
"0.1.2"

--- id tuples/multiplying-every-segment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold 1.2.3 * 2
--- result
"2.4.6"

--- id tuples/dividing-truncates-each-segment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Segments are whole numbers, so 3 over 2 is 1 rather than 1.5.
--- code
mold 1.2.3 / 2
--- result
"0.1.1"

--- id tuples/adding-two-tuples
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold 1.2.3 + 1.1.1
--- result
"2.3.4"

--- id tuples/a-segment-cannot-go-above-its-ceiling
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note It clamps rather than wrapping, so the answer is unchanged
--- note rather than 0.0.0. A wrapping implementation is right for
--- note every value except the ones at the edge.
--- code
mold 255.255.255 + 1
--- result
"255.255.255"

--- id tuples/nor-below-its-floor
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold 0.0.0 - 1
--- result
"0.0.0"

--- id tuples/how-many-segments
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
length? 1.2.3
--- result
3

--- id tuples/the-first-segment-by-path
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
u: 1.2.3
u/1
--- result
1

--- id tuples/the-last-segment-by-path
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
u: 1.2.3
u/3
--- result
3

--- id tuples/one-past-the-last-segment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note None rather than raising, which is how a series behaves past
--- note its end and not how an object behaves.
--- code
u: 1.2.3
u/4
--- result
_

--- id tuples/the-position-before-the-first
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
u: 1.2.3
u/0
--- result
_

--- id tuples/the-first-segment-by-name
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
first 1.2.3
--- result
1

--- id tuples/picking-a-segment
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
pick 1.2.3 2
--- result
2

--- id tuples/two-equal-tuples
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1.2.3 = 1.2.3
--- result
#(true)

--- id tuples/comparing-two-tuples
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
1.2.3 < 1.2.4
--- result
#(true)

--- id tuples/made-from-a-block-of-numbers
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold to tuple! [1 2 3]
--- result
"1.2.3"

--- id tuples/converted-to-a-block-wraps-rather-than-splits
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The same as a pair, and the same surprise.
--- code
mold to block! 1.2.3
--- result
"[1.2.3]"
